              "name": "Session Management Issues",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Problems with how user sessions are created, maintained, and terminated"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "**Session Management Issues**\n\nProblems with how user sessions are created, maintained, and terminated\n\n**Impact (type metadata)**\nAccount takeover, session hijacking, and unauthorized access to user accounts\n\n**Mitigation (type metadata)**\nImplement secure session handling, use proper timeout settings, and protect session tokens"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/psyray/oasis"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "session-management-issues",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Insecure Session ID Generation\n\nThe contract uses a fixed value (0x1) as the session ID in the `initMultiowned` function, which is not cryptographically secure.\n\nImpact: An attacker could potentially manipulate the session ID to gain unauthorized access to the wallet.\n\nRemediation: Use a cryptographically secure method to generate unique session IDs, such as using a salt and a random number."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "/work/project/dataset/vulnerable/access-control/parity_wallet_bug_1.sol"
                },
                "region": {
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "function initMultiowned(address[] _owners, uint _required) { ... }"
                  },
                  "startLine": 1,
                  "endLine": 281
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "oasisModel": "llama3.2:3b",
            "oasisFileSimilarity": 0.6579055143249387,
            "oasisChunkIndex": 0,
