        {
          "ruleId": "session-management-issues",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Vulnerability found\n\nThe revoke function does not properly handle the case when an owner tries to revoke a transaction that has already been confirmed by another owner.\n\nImpact: An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a revoke request for a transaction that has already been confirmed by another owner.\n\nRemediation: The revoke function should be modified to properly handle confirmed transactions."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "/work/project/dataset/vulnerable/access-control/parity_wallet_bug_1.sol"
                },
                "region": {
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "function revoke(bytes32 _operation) external {\n  \\u0002\n  uint ownerIndex = m_ownerIndex[uint(msg.sender)];\n  \\u0003\\n  if (ownerIndex == 0) return;\n  \\u0005\\n  var pending = m_pending[_operation];\n  \\u0007\\n  if (pending.ownersDone & ownerIndexBit > 0) {\n    pending.yetNeeded++;\n    pending.ownersDone -= ownerIndexBit;\n    Revoke(msg.sender, _operation);\n  }\n}"
                  },
                  "startLine": 134,
                  "endLine": 134
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "oasisModel": "llama3.2:3b",
            "oasisFileSimilarity": 0.6579055143249387,
            "oasisChunkIndex": 1,
            "oasisFindingIndex": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "session-management-issues",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Vulnerability found\n\nThe use of `onlymanyowners` with SHA-3 hash from `msg.data` makes the contract vulnerable to session hijacking. An attacker can manipulate the `msg.data` to get a valid signature, allowing them to confirm transactions without actually owning the wallet.\n\nImpact: Account takeover and unauthorized access to user accounts\n\nRemediation: Use `onlymanyowners` with a fixed, predictable transaction hash instead of relying on SHA-3 from user input."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "/work/project/dataset/vulnerable/access-control/parity_wallet_bug_1.sol"
                },
                "region": {
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "function confirm(bytes32 _h) onlymanyowners(sha3(msg.data)) returns (bool o_success) { ... }"
                  },
                  "startLine": 27,
                  "endLine": 358
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
